        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/dom-xss-via-html-injection-sinks-dangerouslysetinnerhtml-innerhtml-eval",
          "ruleIndex": 7,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "DOM-XSS via HTML injection sinks (dangerouslySetInnerHTML/innerHTML/eval) — Ruled out: /assets/index-B22VnECO.js (mindguard.site SPA bundle) — HTML/JS sink audit\n\nStatic: grep of beautified bundle (209KB, 9601 lines) found all 13 dangerouslySetInnerHTML hits are React 18 library internals (prop plumbing at lines 752/1158/1320/4834/4843/5017/5501), zero app-level `__html` usage, zero eval/new Function/document.write/insertAdjacentHTML/`.html()`. Dynamic: payload navigations (`#<img src=x onerror=window.__t1=1>` encoded and raw, `<svg onload>` family) left window markers undefined and payload strings never present in document.body.innerHTML. CSP is only `upgrade-insecure-requests` (no script-src), but no reachable sink exists to exploit."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "/assets/index-B22VnECO.js (mindguard.site SPA bundle) — HTML/JS sink audit"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "ruled_out",
              "risk_area": "DOM-XSS via HTML injection sinks (dangerouslySetInnerHTML/innerHTML/eval)",
              "surface": "/assets/index-B22VnECO.js (mindguard.site SPA bundle) — HTML/JS sink audit",
              "recorded_by": "DOM-XSS & Client-Side Agent",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/dom-xss-via-url-parameter-query-string-injection-into-dom",
          "ruleIndex": 8,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "DOM-XSS via URL parameter (query string) injection into DOM — Ruled out: ?lang= URL parameter handling (mindguard.site Zf/Zf language provider)\n\nStatic: `Zf()` at beautified line 7609 reads `new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get(\"lang\")` but returns the value only if it === \"es\" or === \"en\", else falls back to the localStorage value under the same allowlist, else \"es\". No other URL parameter is read anywhere in the bundle. Dynamic: GET /?lang=<img src=x onerror=window.__t2=1> (proxy id 7772) returned 200 with identical response length to baseline (1927 B, id 7653); marker window.__t2 stayed undefined; localStorage value stayed null."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "?lang= URL parameter handling (mindguard.site Zf/Zf language provider)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "ruled_out",
              "risk_area": "DOM-XSS via URL parameter (query string) injection into DOM",
              "surface": "?lang= URL parameter handling (mindguard.site Zf/Zf language provider)",
              "recorded_by": "DOM-XSS & Client-Side Agent",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/dom-xss-via-location-hash-postmessage-message-handlers",
          "ruleIndex": 9,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "DOM-XSS via location.hash / postMessage message handlers — Ruled out: URL hash routing & postMessage listener surface (mindguard.site anchors)\n\nStatic: zero `location.hash` reads in the bundle (grep count 0), zero `window.addEventListener(\"message\")` / `onmessage` handlers; the only `postMessage` call (line 582) is the React scheduler MessageChannel internal `port2.postMessage(null)`, not a cross-origin receiver. Dynamic: navigations with encoded and raw `<img src=x onerror>` / `<svg onload>` hashes — window markers stayed undefined, `document.body.innerHTML.includes('<img')` false. All anchor hrefs are hardcoded constants (`#top #platform #method #cases #security #faq #contact` + `https://mindguardredteam.com`); no hash value is ever written into the DOM."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "URL hash routing & postMessage listener surface (mindguard.site anchors)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
