          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Client-side storage secrets / persistence vectors — No issue identified: localStorage / sessionStorage / indexedDB / cookie usage (mindguard.site client)\n\nRuntime: `Object.keys(localStorage)` = [] and `Object.keys(sessionStorage)` = [] after the app fully loaded (after I removed the single test value I had written via eval); `document.cookie` = empty; `indexedDB` present as a browser API but bundle grep shows zero indexedDB usage. The only localStorage key the code touches is `mindguard-landing-language` with an es/en allowlist on both read (Zf line 7611) and write (Jf line 7623). A poisoned value (`<img src=x onerror=...`) injected via devtools was read on reload but never entered the DOM (allowlist rejected it, fell back to \"es\"). No secrets, tokens, or PII stored client-side; confirms recon note dfa9ef."
          },
          "locations": [
