          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/service-worker-persistence-script-injection-via-dynamic-src",
          "ruleIndex": 12,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Service worker / persistence / script injection via dynamic src — Ruled out: Cal.com embed loader & dynamic script injection (mindguard.site Vo/Op/Dp functions)\n\nBundle grep for `serviceWorker|register(|Worker(|importScripts|manifest` — zero hits. Only dynamic script injection in the bundle is the Cal.com embed snippet at line 9398 (`i.head.appendChild(i.createElement(\"script\")).src = n`) where `n` derives from the hardcoded constant `https://app.cal.com/embed/embed.js` — not attacker-controllable. Runtime check: document has exactly 2 script elements with those fixed srcs. Cal.com iframe src is a static URL with no user-influenced parameters (`layout/theme/embedType` are fixed values)."
          },
