        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/subdomain-takeover-dangling-dns",
          "ruleIndex": 3,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Subdomain takeover / dangling DNS — Ruled out: redteam.mindguard.site (DNS takeover assessment)\n\nAuthoritative nameservers (aurora/nebula.dns-parking.com, Hostinger) return NXDOMAIN with zero records (no A, no CNAME, no NS delegation) for redteam.mindguard.site, confirmed from 3 public resolvers (1.1.1.1, 8.8.8.8, 9.9.9.9) and directly against NS at 172.64.52.197. A takeover requires a dangling record (CNAME/NS) to a claimable third-party resource; here the DNS record is fully deleted, so there is nothing to claim. CT log (certspotter id 17324447351-range, issued 2026-09-22) shows a cert once existed for redteam.mindguard.site + www.redteam.mindguard.site, but no archived HTTP history (Wayback CDX empty) and no observable prior CNAME target. Named control that makes this safe: the zone simply contains no record for the label, so no attacker-controlled claim can be bound."
          },
          "locations": [
